# Code quality

`strict` TypeScript stays on. External input is validated with Zod at the boundary. Leave `any`, `@ts-ignore`, and non-null assertions out of the code.

Each feature lives in `src/features/<feature>` and owns its components, schemas, queries, and server actions. Files in `src/app` stay thin and delegate to that feature or to `src/server/services`.

```ts
// Bad
const amount = payload!.price as any;

// Good
const amount = priceSchema.parse(payload).amount;
```
